From a2deecdae36d6a28cfa82e90e06c5ca6bde1afaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:14:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GLES] The SDR that Kodi draws itself takes the
 display's 3D LUT; the DRM PRIME decoder says it does not

The 3D LUT for SDR went only on what the bridge maps or draws: the SDR
videos that Kodi's own renderer draws (decoded by the processor, or by
VAAPI, without an upscaler: most of them) were left without it, and the
player information said "not applied: drawn by Kodi".

Taking those videos to the bridge was measured against this and left
aside: the bridge takes no 8-bit picture of the processor (Kodi uploads it
as LUMINANCE and ALPHA, which libplacebo does not wrap), nor an interlaced
or 3D picture, nor Kodi's brightness and contrast, and it scales with its
own scaler, chroma and dither, so that every picture would have changed
besides the LUT, at the cost of a pass of its own. Kodi's own shaders draw
all of them as before, and the LUT is a few reads of a table in the pass
that writes the picture.

CLinuxRendererGLES (and CRendererVAAPIGLES with it) asks the window system
for the LUT of each picture that it draws into the window, as the bridges
do (CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::LutFor(), DisplayLut.h): HDR passed through
to the display takes none (the display maps it: Output::KODI_HDR now says
so), and anything else that it draws goes out as SDR and takes the LUT
for SDR (an SDR video, HDR tone mapped by Kodi's shaders, HLG drawn as
SDR), in the primaries that the shaders draw it in (an SDR output of
BT.2020 or of a wider container takes a LUT made for it, or is refused as
the bridge refuses it). The same LUT as the bridges', read and checked
once, of the display in use. Its table goes to the GPU once for each LUT
(dvbridge_lut_atlas.h, said in kodi.log with its size and time), and the
shaders are made again only where a LUT comes or goes (taken before the
shaders are first made, so that a video starts with them made once). A
shader that this GPU does not make with the LUT is made without it (before
the chroma is stepped down: a LUT is no reason to draw the chroma another
way), the LUT is not tried again for the video, and kodi.log, the notice
and the player information say so. A picture drawn elsewhere than into the
window (a capture) takes none and says nothing. Without a LUT nothing is
inserted, bound or set: the shaders and the pictures are those before.

The videos of the DRM PRIME decoder (videoplayer.useprimedecoder, hidden
and off on this build) have no pass of Kodi's video shaders: their
renderers say so (Output::PRIME, "not applied: DRM PRIME decoder" in the
player information, kodi.log), and the user is asked once a run whether to
turn that decoder off so that the LUT is applied from the next video ("No"
by default leaves it on). The line of the player information is now what
the renderer of the video decided, never a guess for a video that no
bridge drew.

The help of the setting says that the LUT for SDR goes on SDR videos, and
that the menus and subtitles are not corrected, as with Kodi's own colour
management on a desktop.

Strings: core #62802, #62816 and #62820 (en_gb), Estuary #54802, #54816 and
#54820 (en_gb, es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
